rIC3 (portfolio of IC3/BMC/k-induction) returns UNSAT (piece proved), SAT (counterexample; replayed on the concrete model: real if it reproduces, spurious otherwise) or TIMEOUT. The cap per piece is short (3 s at first, longer in later rounds), so a timeout means "not easy yet", not "impossible". Prefer fewer free values: when refining, prefer enable or slice over restoring a whole signal.

